Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:

$$
u=\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}
$$

First, let's compute the sum:

$$
\begin{aligned}
2a+b &= 2\cdot \begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 3\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}8 \\ -12\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}0 \\ 6\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}8 \\ -12\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}0+(8) \\ (6)+(-12)\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}8 \\ -6\end{bmatrix}
\end{aligned}
$$

Using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}
|2a+b| &= \sqrt{(8)^2+(-6)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{100} \\
&= 10
\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:

$$
\begin{aligned}
u &= \frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\
&= \frac{1}{10}\cdot (2a+b) \\
&= \frac{1}{10}\cdot \begin{bmatrix}8 \\ -6\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}\frac{4}{5} \\ - \frac{3}{5}\end{bmatrix}
\end{aligned}
$$

